# Local scratch and run artifacts. These are NOT packaging inputs, and leaving
# them untracked-and-unignored is actively harmful rather than merely untidy:
# every untracked path enters the `git-delta-v1` source-tree fingerprint, so one
# scratch file appearing in lab/out/ invalidates a just-minted current-tree
# re-verification receipt and turns `tools/validate.py --gate ship` red again
# minutes after it was green. Measured 2026-10-04 while closing the future_gate
# waves; the fix is to ignore the scratch surface, not to stop measuring.
lab/out/
lab/*.tmp

# Receiver-local SAIPEN state explicitly marked non-exportable by MANIFEST.
.saipen/locks/
.saipen/recovery/
.saipen/LOCAL_STATE.json

# The canonical SAIMAIL workspace holding this project's durable future letters.
# Receiver-local identity material (private keys under raw custody) plus the
# sealed letter mailboxes.
.saimail-workspace/

# Bootstrap bundles that ship a decryption key NEXT TO the ciphertext it opens.
# An earlier version of this comment called operator_import/future_letters/
# "portable evidence", implying it belonged in the repository. That was wrong,
# and it was wrong in the dangerous direction: the one bundle there,
# SAIMAIL_FUTURE_LETTER_GPT56SOL_20261003_1535.zip, carries RECOVERY_KEY.txt
# (a 32-byte AES-256-GCM key plus its SHA-256) in the same archive as
# FUTURE_LETTER.encrypted.json, which is exactly what that key decrypts.
# Committing it would publish the plaintext of a letter that is sealed only in
# the sense that its key travels with it. Ignored, not staged.
operator_import/future_letters/*.zip

# Scratch from tools that are not part of this project, and a stray empty file.
.freebuff/
canonical
